# Workspace

This workspace uses the [ai-workspace plugin](https://github.com/sebmartin/ai-workspace-plugin) for thread-based conversation management.

## Threads

Threads are organized conversations stored in `threads/`. Each thread has its own README, session logs, decisions, and artifacts.

Use natural language to manage them, or the explicit commands below.

### Archived threads are read-only

Archiving moves a thread from `threads/` to `archive/`. It keeps its shape there, so an
archived thread looks exactly like a live one.

**Read an archived thread when asked. Never write to one.** To work on an archived thread,
restore it first, which moves it back into `threads/`.

**Claude Code:**

```
/ai-workspace:threads create <name>   # Start a new thread
/ai-workspace:threads resume <name>   # Resume a thread mid-session
/ai-workspace:threads                 # List all threads
```

**Codex CLI:**

```
/threads create <name>
/threads resume <name>
/threads
```

Or just describe what you want, both clients understand natural language.
